            <ArticleTitle>[Lymphocytes B and NK in respiratory allergy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>183-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">High affinity immunoglobulin E (IgE) receptors may activate the mast cell degradation; on the other hand, the ones of low affinity may activate B lymphocytes so they act as antigen-presenting cells and as producers of the same immunoglobulin. As allergic patients produce a great quantity of IgE they are prone to get an infection.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To quantify the IgE increase in 28 patients with allergic rhinitis or asthma, or both without having received a previous treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">38 patients with allergic rhinitis, bronchial asthma, allergic conjunctivitis or atopic dermatitis diagnosis were included. B lymphocytes and NK cells immunophenotypification was made. Flow cytometry was used for cells lecture. Data were analyzed with descriptive statistics applying central tendency measurements.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">No variations were found in the values of any cell lineage.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Proliferation and activation of B lymphocytes should be considered in allergic diseases as its quantification in serum may be a measurement parameter of allergic activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
